---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import PublicLayout from '../../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';

const alternatePaths = { it: '/security/', en: '/en/security/' };
const claims = await getCollection('claims', ({ data }) => data.locales.includes('en') && (data.status === 'live' || data.status === 'beta'));
---

<PublicLayout lang="en" title="Security and data" description="Groowy's security perimeter: minimisation, local data and public claims linked to evidence." canonicalPath="/en/security/" {alternatePaths}>
  <article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Security</p><h1>The useful data is the necessary data.</h1><p>This page separates what is verified today from what is still being prepared: where data starts, which features can move it and which residues must stay outside the product perimeter.</p><div class="notice">This page is not a PCI certification, legal guarantee or promise of absolute security. It is a record of technical behaviour verified on the stated date.</div><section class="card data-card" aria-labelledby="data-orientation-title"><h2 id="data-orientation-title">A quick data orientation</h2><dl class="data-facts"><div><dt>What</dt><dd>Transactions, documents and references you choose to manage; external features add only the data needed for their use case.</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>The personal base starts on the device. Cloud, AI, Groups and Drive enter only when you activate the relevant feature.</dd></div><div><dt>How long</dt><dd>Duration depends on the feature and provider; the full policy describes retention, backups and deletion.</dd></div><div><dt>Control</dt><dd>You can choose, revoke or disable available features and use the provided export or deletion flows.</dd></div></dl><p class="microcopy"><a href="/privacy/">Read the full privacy notice</a>: this card is an orientation, not a replacement for the legal text.</p></section><div class="claim-list">{claims.map((claim) => (<article class="card"><div class="claim-meta"><span class="badge">{claim.data.status}</span><span>{claim.data.claimId}</span><span>verified {claim.data.verifiedAt}</span></div><h2>{claim.data.titleEn ?? claim.data.title}</h2><p>{claim.data.descriptionEn ?? claim.data.description}</p><ul class="evidence">{claim.data.evidenceRefs.map((reference) => <li>{reference}</li>)}</ul></article>))}</div><h2>Payment cards: minimum perimeter</h2><p>For the release candidate, the direction is to treat a payment card as a minimal visual reference, not as a credential wallet.</p><ul><li>retain only network/issuer and, if genuinely useful, the last four digits;</li><li>never retain full PAN, CVC/CVV, PIN, magnetic-stripe or chip data;</li><li>do not persist front/back images or raw OCR; cloud OCR for payment remains excluded until the path is verified end to end.</li></ul></article>
</PublicLayout>
